@startuml
title CETP Client — Component / Module Dependencies

package "konnektor-soap-server" {
  [KonnektorEventService] as EvtSvc
}

package "cetp-client-lib" {
  [CetpClient] as CC
  [SubscriptionService] as SS
  [KonnektorSystemEvent\n(CDI event record)] as Evt
  package "filter" {
    [EventDeliveryFilter] as IF
    [TopicPrefixFilter] as F1
    [AccessAuthorizationFilter] as F2
    [XPathExpressionFilter] as F3
  }
  package "delivery" {
    [CetpEventSender] as Sender
    [CetpFrameCodec] as Codec
    [EventXmlWriter] as XmlW
  }
  package "subscription (JPA)" {
    [Subscription] as Sub
    [ClientEndpoint] as Ep
  }
  package "tls" {
    [CetpTlsContextFactory] as TlsF
  }
}

package "konnektor-soap-server" {
  [CetpClientIdentityProducer] as KidProd
}
package "quarkus-sicct-extension" {
  [SmkCSAKAut] as Smk
}
package "api-telematik" {
  [eventservice.v7 JAXB\n(Event)] as Jaxb
}

EvtSvc --> SS
EvtSvc ..> Sub : persists via SS
Evt ..> CC : @ObservesAsync
CC --> SS : valid subscriptions
CC --> IF
IF <|.. F1
IF <|.. F2
IF <|.. F3
CC --> Sender
Sender --> Codec
Sender --> XmlW
Sender --> TlsF
XmlW --> Jaxb
TlsF ..> KidProd : @KonnektorClientIdentity\nKeyManagerFactory (CDI)
KidProd --> Smk
SS --> Sub
SS --> Ep
Sub --> Ep : @ManyToOne

note bottom of TlsF
  Standard JSSE SSLContext:
  keyManager = @KonnektorClientIdentity KeyManagerFactory (from SmkCSAKAut),
  trustManager = TrustManagerFactory("PKIX") over the client-system trust store.
  Delivery uses JDK Socket / SSLSocket (one connection per delivery).
end note

note top of KidProd
  konnektor-soap-server produces the @KonnektorClientIdentity
  KeyManagerFactory from SmkCSAKAut, so cetp-client-lib stays
  decoupled from quarkus-sicct-extension.
end note
@enduml
